CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_THE_MOMUS_INTRO	"Falamar."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]There was nothing but darkness.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Falamar."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]I twisted in my dreams. I still imagined the tentacle around my leg through the veil of fear and emptiness. I drifted toward eternal sleep, but something wouldn't let me go.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Falamar."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]I opened my eyes and there was water all around, a world without earth or sky. I floated weightless in the current, forever falling in the seas caress.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]There was another above me, a woman, but as inhuman as she was beautiful. She was the tide, powerful but yielding, fleeting but eternal.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Who are you?" I asked.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I am Condatis, the archangel of Danalin, God of the Sea."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Afraid, I tried to swim away from her. I wasn't religious but I had seen enough temples and asylums of those that worshiped Danalin to suspect that this wasn't the afterlife I intended. Even if it did feature floating billowy maidens.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Danalin? As in the Undertow? Is this the heaven for cultists and zealots?"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]She looked hurt. There was pain in her eyes, and love. I regretted my words.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"No." she replied.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Oh... are you my reward?"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"No!" she said, this time there was anger in her eyes.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]I seemed to be getting this all wrong so I just floated silently and let her speak.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I led you to Keelyn so that she would take you to her father, but Hastur predicts my actions. An archmage, Tebryn Arbandi, means to destroy creation. Go to the Momus, convince him to supply you with a fleet then sail through the Arduro Straight to the Dead Lands. Defeat Tebryn so I have time to defeat Hastur."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"You sure you don't want Capria, or that guy that killed Mulcarn? I'm more of a steal-the-king's-galleon kind of hero."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]She smiled, "My young prince, we must all make do with what we have."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][NEWLINE]The water rippled and her face was replaced with the bearded face of Amergin. He was pulling me up on the beach.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Falamar, are you okay?"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I'm okay," I stammered through racking coughs, "how are the men?"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Some are fine, others haven't been recovered yet."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]I understood his meaning and picked myself up. After recovering far too few of my men from the sea we went to meet with Perpentach. He ignored the threat of Tebryn and my pleas for help. But he was holding a competition between warlords, and he promised to supply the navy I required if I won. With few men and no ships, we had little choice but to enter.	法拉玛。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]除了黑暗，一无所有。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"法拉玛。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]我在梦中辗转。透过那层恐惧与空虚的帷幕，我仍觉得有一条触须缠着我的腿。我朝着永恒的长眠漂去，却有什么不肯放我离去。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"法拉玛。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]我睁开眼，四周尽是海水，一个没有大地也没有天空的世界。我在水流中失重地漂浮，永远坠落在大海的爱抚里。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]我上方另有一人，一位女子，她既美丽又不似凡人。她是潮汐，强大却柔顺，短暂却永恒。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"你是谁？"我问。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我是孔达提斯，海神达纳林的大天使。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]我心生惧意，试图从她身边游开。我并不虔信，但我见过够多崇拜达纳林之人的神庙与庇护所，足以怀疑这并非我所愿的死后之境。哪怕它当真有飘浮的曼妙少女相伴。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"达纳林？就是那‘暗流’的达纳林？这里莫非是邪教徒和狂信者的天堂？"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]她似乎受了伤。她眼中有痛楚，也有爱意。我为自己的话感到懊悔。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"不是，"她答道。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"哦……那你是我的犒赏？"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"不是！"她说，这一次她眼里带着怒意。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]我似乎全说错了，于是只好静静漂着，任她言说。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我引你去往琪琳身边，好让她带你去见她父亲，可哈斯图尔预见了我的举动。一位大魔法师，特布里恩·阿尔班第，意欲摧毁造化。去找莫姆斯，说服他为你提供一支舰队，然后穿越阿杜罗海峡驶向亡者之地。击败特布里恩，好让我有时间去击败哈斯图尔。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"你确定不想要凯布瑞尔，或是那个杀了穆尔卡恩的家伙？我更像是那种偷国王大帆船的英雄。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]她微笑道，"我年轻的王子，我们都得将就着用手上现有的。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][NEWLINE]水波荡漾，她的面容被阿默金那张满是胡须的脸取代。他正把我拖上沙滩。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"法拉玛，你没事吧？"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我没事，"我剧烈咳嗽着结结巴巴地说，"弟兄们怎么样了？"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"有些没事，还有些尚未寻回。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]我明白他的意思，撑起身子。从海里寻回的弟兄少得可怜，此后我们便去与普宾塔克会面。他无视特布里恩的威胁，也无视我求援的恳请。但他正举办一场群雄之间的竞赛，并承诺若我获胜，便供我所需的舰队。手下人马寥寥，又无船只，我们别无多少选择，只得参赛。
CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_THE_SPLINTERED_COURT_VICTORY_LJOSALFAR	Faeryl was laid to rest with the honors due an elven queen. Though many argued against a funeral for an enemy leader, Arendel had demanded it. As controversial as it had been no one questioned it now and the massive funeral was properly somber and respectful.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Of the former Svartalfar, all those that had sworn allegiance to the summer court were invited to attend. For the first time in two ages the Svartalfar and Ljosalfar united in a common task, even if it was to mourn the death of the winter queen. They stood up and eulogized her and Svartalfar and Ljosalfar alike shed tears for Faeryl. Even Arendel stood and spoke lovingly of her sister, the fallen queen.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]That night the funeral procession passed through the streets of Evermore as starlight glistened off of the silver and mithril coffin. As was tradition her coffin was displayed within the Sacred Grove for the night and then moved to the hidden tomb used to house elven royalty in the morning. By then thousands of gifts were brought to the temple and laid around the tomb.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Just before dawn horns summoned all the citizens of Evermore to the city's grand plaza. Once everyone was gathered Arendel came out onto the palace balcony and addressed them.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"We must not forget. We must not forget our legends, the days spent within this very wood as the children of Sucellus and Cernunnos. We must not forget that age we spent on our own as a single elven nation and the trials and fortune we shared. And we must not forget that we turned to war with each other."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Every memory we have is shared, every glory, every defeat. We are one people, and we were even as we killed each other."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Long ago, Sucellus anointed two queens to lead us so that the passions of one person could not lead our empire into ruin as happened with the empire of men. But this split led to civil war."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Through prayer and careful deliberation with the priests, sages and captains of both former empires we have decided to form a new high council. That there would be two elven queens and an elven king to lead us. That these leaders would rule year round within their own nations and that they would come together to decide matters for the empire."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I will be the queen of Evermore, of the temples and over the monuments and artifacts of our empire. I will tend to the orchards and provide for the musicians, artists and craftsmen. Brave Amelanchier will be anointed as king and assigned our army, given provision over our forts and made responsible for our defense. He will also take charge of our hunters and be responsible for the lands untended within our borders. Thessa will be anointed as queen and responsible for all manners of study, arcane or mundane, as well as diplomacy and trade with other lands. If military action is to occur outside of our empire then it will be under her leadership."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"If you are a child of Sucellus then you are a member of our empire. A particular faith is not a requirement and the former Svartalfar are equal in every way to other citizens. The war is over and if we are to shed tears then we must do so together. If we are angry then we must be angry with ourselves. As mighty Sucellus was destroyed by winter and split apart until Nantosuelta gathered his pieces back together for his resurrection, so are the Ljosalfar. Now rejoined we are reborn, and I pray that will ever be so."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]As dawn struck the plaza the Ljosalfar palace seemed to glow with an aura of gold and white. It was a new world for the Ljosalfar and they couldn't help but feel hopeful that it would be a kinder world than they had known for centuries.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][NEWLINE]That night, after to coronation of Thessa and Amelanchier and seeing them off to their remote capitals Arendel retired to her personal chambers. After checking the magical wards that protected the rooms she removed her amulet and watched in the mirror as the illusion melted away. Her long blond hair shortened to wavy black. Her skin paled to cool alabaster. Her body shifted from the lean beautiful form of the elven queen to her own more sensual and curved body.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Far away, beneath the great red oak of Evermore, within the hidden tomb for elven royalty, behind powerful guards and locked within a silver and mithril box the real Arendel screamed.	菲尔蕾尔以一位精灵女王应得的礼遇入土为安。尽管许多人反对为敌方领袖举行葬礼，阿伦德尔却坚持要办。虽曾颇具争议，如今却无人再有异议，这场盛大的葬礼办得庄重而恭敬，恰如其分。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]昔日的斯瓦塔尔法之中，凡宣誓效忠夏庭者，皆受邀出席。两个纪元以来，斯瓦塔尔法与勒约沙尔法首次为一件共同之事而联合，哪怕这件事是为悼念冬之女王的逝去。他们起身为她致悼词，斯瓦塔尔法与勒约沙尔法都为菲尔蕾尔洒下热泪。就连阿伦德尔也起身，深情地追念她的姊妹，那位陨落的女王。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]那一夜，送葬的队伍穿过永恒之城的街道，星光在那银与秘银铸就的棺椁上熠熠生辉。依照传统，她的棺椁在圣林中停灵一夜，翌日清晨再移入用以安放精灵王族的隐秘陵墓。到那时，已有数以千计的祭品被送到神庙，环绕陵墓摆放。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]黎明将至，号角召集永恒之城所有市民聚集到城中的大广场。待众人齐集，阿伦德尔来到宫殿的阳台上，向他们训话。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我们不可忘记。我们不可忘记我们的传说，忘记我们身为苏塞卢斯与刻努诺斯之子，在这片林中度过的岁月。我们不可忘记那个我们作为单一精灵民族独自度过的纪元，忘记我们共担的磨难与共享的福泽。我们更不可忘记，我们曾兵戈相向。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我们所有的记忆都是共有的，每一份荣耀，每一次挫败。我们是同一族人，纵使在彼此残杀之时也是如此。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"很久以前，苏塞卢斯册立两位女王来统领我们，好叫一人的私欲不致像人类帝国那般把我们的帝国引向毁灭。但这一分立却招致了内战。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"经过祷告，以及与两个昔日帝国的祭司、贤者与将领悉心商议，我们决定组建一个新的高等议会。设两位精灵女王与一位精灵国王来统领我们。这些领袖终年在各自的邦国内治理，又聚在一起共议帝国之事。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我将做永恒之城的女王，掌管神庙、纪念碑与帝国的器物。我将照料果园，供养乐师、艺人与匠人。勇敢的阿米兰伽埃尔将被册立为王，统领我们的军队，掌管我们的堡垒，负责我们的防务。他还将主管我们的猎手，负责我们疆域内无人照管的土地。塞莎将被册立为女王，负责一切研习之事，无论是奥术还是俗务，并负责与他邦的外交与贸易。若要在我们帝国之外采取军事行动，则由她统领。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"你若是苏塞卢斯之子，你便是我们帝国的一员。特定的信仰并非必需，昔日的斯瓦塔尔法在一切方面都与其他公民平等。战争已经结束，若我们要洒泪，就必须一同落泪。若我们心怀愤怒，就必须对自己愤怒。正如伟大的苏塞卢斯被寒冬摧毁、四分五裂，直到南托苏尔塔将他的碎片重新聚拢使他复活，勒约沙尔法亦是如此。如今重新合一，我们便获得重生，我愿它永远如此。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]黎明降临广场时，勒约沙尔法的宫殿仿佛笼罩着一层金白色的光晕。这是勒约沙尔法的一个新世界，他们不禁满怀希望，盼它会是一个比他们数百年来所知的更为仁慈的世界。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][NEWLINE]那一夜，塞莎与阿米兰伽埃尔加冕之后，送走他们前往各自偏远的都城，阿伦德尔便退回自己的寝殿。查看过守护房间的魔法结界后，她取下自己的护符，望着镜中的幻象层层褪去。她那长长的金发缩短为波浪状的黑发。她的肤色苍白为清冷的雪花石白。她的身形从精灵女王那清瘦秀美的模样，变回她自己更加丰腴妖娆的曲线之躯。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]在遥远之处，永恒之城那棵巨大红橡之下，安放精灵王族的隐秘陵墓之中，重重强力守卫之后，被锁在一只银与秘银铸就的匣子里，真正的阿伦德尔发出尖叫。
CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_WAGES_OF_SIN_CONCLUSION_CALABIM	Flauros had come to observe the progress Decius was making, and they consulted over dinner. Decius was eating the last stores of an elven city recently conquered, as it was getting harder to find decent food as Hyborem's corruption spread. Flauros merely sipped his imported wine. A fire crackled as they discussed the final battle plans, causing shadows to dance on the castle's walls.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]One of the shadows detached itself, however, and dove towards Decius, knives in each hand. One pierced the warrior's side, and he fell from his chair. Flauros watched calmly as Decius rolled aside and removed the knife. The wound wasn't bad, due to his light armor. The assassin lunged again, and Decius barely moved aside. He grabbed the man's arm and swung him into the wall, stunning him with a sickening crunch.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Flauros pushed himself back from the table and rose. "Very well done, my friend. With this invader as well as the entire Tempus Mor gambit. They say the best revenge is living well. I think you've earned the gift. Take this man's dying blood and I will show you the ritual we use to prolong our lives."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Decius gazed at the cloaked man for a moment, then drew his blade and plunged it into the assassin's heart. Flauros smiled, but Decius cut him off with a "No."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"You are refusing the gift?"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Yes, I am. If I were to live forever, I might end up like you. Weak and soft."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]His patron replied by picking up the assassin and tearing his head off with his bare hands.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Decius continued, "You have physical strength, but you take it for granted. The cunning hunter has become the fat and lazy shepherd. Your immortality makes you content to sit back and let the world pass you by. I have walked alongside death and am not ready to abandon him now; I need this foe to keep my reflexes sharp and my plans focused."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Flauros studied Decius for a moment, then replied, "You no longer amuse me. I am returning to Prespur. You may do as you wish with those who will follow you, but do not return to my city on pain of death."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Decius watched Flauros left, then smiled to himself. He turned to the dead assassin and said, "Now, that's a useful trick you have. Wonder if there are any more like you?"	弗劳诺斯前来查看德西乌斯的进展，二人在晚宴上商议。德西乌斯正吃着一座新近攻陷的精灵城市所剩的最后一点存粮，因为随着海勃雷姆的腐蚀蔓延，像样的食物越来越难寻。弗劳诺斯只是啜饮着他进口的葡萄酒。炉火噼啪作响，他们商讨着最后的作战计划，令阴影在城堡的墙上舞动。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]然而，其中一道阴影却脱离出来，扑向德西乌斯，双手各执一柄短刀。一刀刺入这位战士的侧腰，他从椅上跌落。弗劳诺斯镇定地看着德西乌斯翻滚到一旁，拔出短刀。因他身着轻甲，伤势并不重。刺客再度扑来，德西乌斯堪堪闪开。他抓住那人的手臂，将他甩向墙壁，随着一声令人作呕的碎裂声将其击晕。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]弗劳诺斯从桌旁向后一推，起身而立。"干得漂亮，我的朋友。这名入侵者，还有整个坦普斯·摩尔的谋局。人说最好的复仇便是活得精彩。我看你已挣得了这份馈赠。取这人临死之血，我便向你演示我们用来延年益寿的仪式。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]德西乌斯凝视着那名披斗篷之人片刻，随即拔出佩刃，刺入刺客的心脏。弗劳诺斯微微一笑，却被德西乌斯一句"不"打断。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"你是在拒绝这份馈赠？"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"是的，我拒绝。若我永生不死，也许最终会变得像你一样。软弱而怠惰。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]他的庇护者以行动作答——一把抓起那名刺客，赤手将他的头颅撕了下来。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]德西乌斯继续道，"你有一身蛮力，却视之为理所当然。狡黠的猎手，已变成了肥胖懒惰的牧人。你的不朽让你甘于安坐，任世界从你身边流逝。我曾与死亡并肩而行，此刻还不愿弃他而去；我需要这个对手来使我的反应保持敏锐，我的谋划保持专注。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]弗劳诺斯端详德西乌斯片刻，随后答道，"你不再令我觉得有趣了。我要回普雷斯普尔去。追随你的那些人，你可随意处置，但若敢再踏入我的城市，格杀勿论。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]德西乌斯目送弗劳诺斯离去，随即暗自一笑。他转向那名已死的刺客，说道，"喏，你这本事倒挺有用。不知还有没有别的像你这样的人？"
CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_WAGES_OF_SIN_CONCLUSION_MALAKIM	Decius directed his army to set up his camp on the foothills of Tempus Mor. The war had been long, and had hardened the Malakim recruits he led, but they stayed true to the Empyrean ideals, and had spared some remnant of his allies' civilizations. The eternal feud between Basium and the Infernals was sure to spread like fire to the rest of the world, as reports came in of Hellfire gates opening in distant lands through the actions of Sheaim agents.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]But Tempus Mor would have peace, and Varn's vision of an alliance of the good nations had borne fruit. Decius set a guard and headed into his tent to plot his next action. After some time he fell asleep on the ground beside his maps.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Late into the night he was awoken by a shout from his guard. As he rose he saw, from nowhere, an assassin's arm, dagger readied. Battle-hardened reflexes saved Decius's life, and he disarmed the assassin only to watch him begin to fade from view again. Whether this was some demon or wizard, Decius knew he had better find out who sent him. He grabbed a torch and swung it at the intruder to disrupt his spell. The assassin, a human man cloaked in grey, fell to the ground screaming and Decius's guards were able to subdue him.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Interrogation revealed an iron will in the assassin, but he was able to rule out the Svartalfar, Infernals, and Calabim as a source. As he mulled over how to get a motive out of his would-be killer, a messenger arrived. An Elohim monk with word that Ethne the White had succumbed to a similar strike, and magic was useless to revive her. If the Elohim ruler was to be restored, her assailant must be tracked down. And ignoring this threat would surely lead to future attempts, which might pierce his defenses. He had hoped to reinforce a city called Bourne the Gleaming, founded by Empyrean missionaries sent shortly after the first council in the desert of Myrh. But this mission south, into the wastes, took priority. With the secrets of the Mercurian Gate that Ethne had given them, they may be able to hold out against the Infernals summoned from the Hell-fire in lands of Os-Gabella's Sheaim ally, Tebryn.	德西乌斯指挥他的军队在坦普斯·摩尔的山麓扎营。这场战争漫长，把他所率的马拉基姆新兵磨砺得坚韧，但他们仍忠于天穹教的理想，还饶过了盟友文明的一些残余。随着报告传来，塞安密探的行动在远方之地开启了一道道地狱之火的大门，巴希姆与地狱军团之间那永恒的宿怨，注定要如烈火般蔓延至世界其余之处。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]但坦普斯·摩尔将迎来和平，范恩所憧憬的善良诸国联盟已然结出硕果。德西乌斯布下岗哨，走进营帐谋划下一步行动。过了一阵，他便在地图旁的地上睡着了。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]夜深时分，他被岗哨的一声呼喊惊醒。起身之际，他看见一只刺客的手臂不知从何处冒出，匕首已然备好。久经沙场的反应救了德西乌斯一命，他缴了刺客的械，却眼看着他又开始从视野中隐去。无论这是恶魔还是巫师，德西乌斯知道他最好查清是谁派来的。他抓起一支火把朝那闯入者挥去，扰乱他的法术。那刺客，一个裹着灰袍的人类男子，尖叫着倒地，德西乌斯的卫兵得以将他制服。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]审讯揭示出这刺客有着钢铁般的意志，但他得以排除斯瓦塔尔法、地狱军团与卡拉比姆作为幕后之源。正当他斟酌该如何从这名意图弑他之人口中套出动机时，一名信使赶到。一名埃洛希姆修士带来消息：白袍艾斯妮已死于一次类似的袭击，魔法也无力将她复活。若要让这位埃洛希姆的统治者复生，就必须追查出袭击她的凶手。而无视这一威胁，日后必将招来更多刺杀，或许会刺穿他的防御。他本盼着去增援一座名叫‘微光者伯尔尼’的城市，那是在密尔沙漠首次议会之后不久，由天穹教传教士所建。但这次南下、深入荒芜之地的行动，才是当务之急。凭借艾斯妮交予他们的天界之门的秘密，他们或许能抵挡住那些从奥斯·加贝拉的塞安盟友特布里恩领地上的地狱之火中召唤而出的地狱军团。
CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_WAGES_OF_SIN_INTRO_MALAKIM	Decius watched the armies of the allied Malakim tribes array into a rough formation, each man with his arms and near his kin. There was much squabbling and joking; far from the ordered troops he had commanded on Bannor crusade. "They are not prepared for what we face, Vaughn."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"We haven't embarked on a religious war before. We have no hardened crusaders among us. I count this a point in favor of the Empyrean, do you not?"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I do not count na&#239;vet&#233; as a virtue when I march to war. Fanaticism is a vice I do not wish to import, but martial discipline will be critical if any of these men are to return."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]The Vicar frowned. "It would be good if we could stay longer in this desert, where we have the advantage. But if our council is to sustain us in our hard times, we must stand with the Elohim in their dark hour."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Indeed. I would prefer to train them more, but what Varn Gosam tells me is cause for immediate mobilization. There is a dark and secretive people known as the Sheaim, and their schemes have reached fruition with an Infernal Pact. Agares's archangel Hyborem has entered our world. He has struck against the Ljosalfar, allowing our old enemies the Svartalfar an advantage in their war. The Elohim have brought in another ally, a force for good but not for peace-the renegade Basium and his warriors. Weakness in this war will bring destruction to the forces of good."	德西乌斯看着结盟的马拉基姆各部大军排成一个粗略的阵形，每人都携着自己的武器，靠着自己的族亲。其间多有争吵与打趣，与他在班诺尔十字军中统率过的那些秩序井然的部队相去甚远。"他们还没准备好面对我们即将遭遇之事，沃恩。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我们此前从未投身宗教战争。我们中没有久经沙场的十字军。我倒觉得这是天穹教的一个长处，你不这么看吗？"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"当我开赴战场时，我不把天真幼稚当作美德。狂热是一种我不愿引入的恶习，但若这些人中有谁想活着回来，军纪将至关重要。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]那位教区代牧皱起眉头。"若我们能在这片占有优势的沙漠里多待些时日，那自然是好。但倘若我们的议会要在艰难时刻扶持我们，我们就必须在埃洛希姆的至暗时刻与他们并肩而立。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"的确。我更愿多加操练他们，但范恩·哥萨姆告诉我的事，足以令我即刻动员。有一支阴暗而隐秘的民族，人称塞安，他们的阴谋已随一纸地狱契约而得逞。阿加雷斯的大天使海勃雷姆已进入我们的世界。他已对勒约沙尔法出手，让我们的宿敌斯瓦塔尔法在他们的战争中占了上风。埃洛希姆已引来另一位盟友，一股为善却不为和平的力量——叛逆者巴希姆及其麾下战士。在这场战争中示弱，将给善的势力带来毁灭。"
CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_WAGES_OF_SIN_TALIA_1_ELOHIM	Ethne traveled to Golden Leane to attend the meeting of the Overcouncil. Usually an envoy went in her place, but after recent gains in their mutual struggle she decided to go in person, especially to address the plight of Sheaim and Svartalfar prisoners of war. The Malakim were a good people, but their new commander Decius struck her as overly... pragmatic. He deferred a great deal to Varn Gosam, however, and the Empyrean patriarch was a merciful elven man.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Chalid was at the council meeting, Varn Gosam's closest disciple, and another non-member: Varn's wife. Ethne greeted her before they formally began. "It is good to see you well, Talia. I think of you often when I hear of the destruction left in the wake of our enemies. There will be much work to do to return our land to order when we win here; perhaps you could aid our efforts in the savannah region Flauros has claimed."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Hmm? Oh, yes. These things trouble us all, of course. In fact, I will get a chance to see this area first hand as an envoy to the Calabim. They are unnatural monsters, but perhaps they can see that aiding this Hell on Erebus is not in their interest."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I'm sure you will be missed here as you travel."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"We all have our roles to fill, Ethne. Our desires cannot interfere with our goals."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I simply meant..." Ethne's voice trailed off as Talia took a seat between Varn and Decius.	艾斯妮前往金色琳恩，出席至高议会的会议。通常由一名使节代她前往，但在双方共同的抗争近来有所斩获之后，她决定亲自前去，尤其是为了处置塞安与斯瓦塔尔法战俘的困境。马拉基姆是善良的一族，但他们的新指挥官德西乌斯却让她觉得过于……务实了。不过他对范恩·哥萨姆颇为尊崇，而这位天穹教的元老是一位仁慈的精灵。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]卡利德也在议会上，他是范恩·哥萨姆最亲近的门徒，还有另一位非成员：范恩的妻子。正式开始之前，艾斯妮向她致意。"见你安好，真是太好了，塔莉亚。每当我听闻敌人所过之处留下的毁灭时，便常常想起你。待我们在此地取胜，要让我们的土地重归秩序，还有许多事要做；也许你可以在弗劳诺斯所占的那片草原地区助我们一臂之力。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"嗯？哦，是啊。这些事自然令我们所有人忧心。事实上，作为出使卡拉比姆的使节，我将有机会亲眼看看那一带。他们是些反常的怪物，但也许他们能看清，助长这伊瑞布斯上的地狱并不符合他们的利益。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"你出行在外，这里定会想念你的。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我们各有各的本分要尽，艾斯妮。我们的私欲不能妨碍我们的目标。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我只是想说……"艾斯妮的话音渐渐低了下去，塔莉亚在范恩与德西乌斯之间落了座。
CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_WAGES_OF_SIN_TALIA_1_SHEAIM	A Svartalfar spy was waiting in Os-Gabella's chambers when she retired for the night. "This game of Faeryl's may intimidate some, but it merely annoys me to have to kill so many of her spies," Os-Gabella said.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"I come with a message, dear friend of the Svartalfar. An opportunity. A tale of conversation overheard in the palace of another friend. The wife of Varn Gosam, a woman of greatly divergent temperament, requests the Calabim withdrawal from our alliance. Decius declines the offer, overly politely. There is more here than diplomacy. A risk that Decius may be swayed, but as far as he has come, he has scant recourse to go back. If she were to have a moment of weakness though, it would stab at the heart of the Overcouncil."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Os-Gabella smiled. "Perhaps if we alienate Decius... make him lonely, to long for a companion, he would seek out this woman in the future. Make sure he knows his fortune depends on his allegiance to us, however."	奥斯·加贝拉夜里就寝时，一名斯瓦塔尔法密探正在她的寝室中等候。"菲尔蕾尔玩的这套把戏或许能吓住一些人，但对我而言，不过是要杀掉她这么多密探，徒增烦扰罢了，"奥斯·加贝拉说道。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"我带来一则消息，斯瓦塔尔法的挚友。一个机会。一段在另一位友人宫中偷听到的对话。范恩·哥萨姆的妻子，一个性情迥异的女子，请求卡拉比姆退出我们的同盟。德西乌斯回绝了这一请求，客气得过了头。这里头不止是外交那么简单。有一种风险，德西乌斯或许会被动摇，可他已走到这一步，几乎没有回头的余地。然而，倘若她有一刻的软弱，那便会刺向至高议会的心脏。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]奥斯·加贝拉微微一笑。"也许，倘若我们疏远德西乌斯……让他变得孤独，渴望有个伴，他日后便会去寻这个女子。不过要确保他明白，他的命运系于他对我们的效忠。"
CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_WB_WAGES_OF_SIN_TALIA_2_SHEAIM	Talia walked unescorted from the Calabim borders through the savannah. It was early morning, and she headed towards the rising sun, towards home. Decius had just released her from a captivity that she had forgotten wasn't voluntary. He had fascinated her, and she had betrayed her husband Varn Gosam to her baser instincts. But she learned much of the man whose armies opposed hers, and she comforted herself with the thought that this information might aid her people in stopping the Calabim.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Do you know how the Sea of Sorrow was named?" The voice came from the shadows of a rock formation as she passed by.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Who's there? I have been granted passage as a prisoner exchange by Decius of the Calabim."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]An old crone in dusty purple robes emerged from the shadows. "There once was a great king who ruled over this land. Lord of all he would survey. His palace stood on a cliff overlooking the sea on the western edge." She paused.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Talia gave her no further prompting. "I have no time for your story. I am too long delayed from my home already." She turned away and hurried on, but found the woman ahead of her.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"It is his sorrow from which this sea draws its name. A great king who had everything he asked for given. And he climbed the tower stairs to throw himself to his death in the crashing sea beneath."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"What concern is this of mine? Kings come and go; all creatures suffer. I must return to my people, who struggle with a threat to every living thing under the sun!" The dust around her feet rose swirling around her, cutting off the old woman, and again Talia turned towards home.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]This time she saw the woman step from thin air in front of her. "What caused a sorrow so great to make him disdain his own life? Do you not know the story?" The Crone looked into Talia's eyes, who this time held her gaze. "That which he most treasured was shown to be false. A promise shown a lie. A wife shown untrue."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"Spirit be gone! Do not... do not judge me."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"The king's greatest desire was for his trusted queen to stand loyally by his side and help him to rule justly. He was too kind to send her away, too wise to trust her again, too idealistic to live with his dream out of reach. His death was the only solution within his grasp."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"It would be better had he never learned of this," Talia said softly.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"He will learn of it," the Crone said.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"He should... he can take another."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"He is too true to do that. The king could not be happy... not while the queen who betrayed him still lived."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]The old woman turned away, releasing Talia from her gaze. Talia shook her head, then turned away, running towards home.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]The crone's ancient fa&#231;ade faded away. She removed a small mirror from her robes, and sprinkled a powder over it, revealing a dreary castle in a hellish landscape. "The seeds are planted, Lethe. Follow this one. Take her guilt and pain as supplication, and lead her to your embrace."[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Then after one final look to the fleeing Talia, Os-Gabella spoke a arcane command and returned to her palace.	塔莉亚独自一人从卡拉比姆边境穿过草原走着。时值清晨，她朝着初升的太阳走去，朝着家的方向。德西乌斯刚刚将她从一场她早已忘了并非出于自愿的囚禁中释放。他曾令她着迷，而她也曾背叛丈夫范恩·哥萨姆，屈从于自己更卑下的本能。但她对这个大军与她为敌之人了解甚多，她安慰自己说，这些情报或许能助她的族人阻止卡拉比姆。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"你可知‘悲伤之海’这名字是怎么来的？"她经过一处岩层时，那声音从阴影中传来。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"是谁？我已获德西乌斯以战俘交换的名义准予通行。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]一个身着满是尘土的紫袍的老妪从阴影中现身。"从前有一位伟大的国王统治着这片土地。他放眼所及，皆归他所有。他的宫殿矗立在西缘一处俯瞰大海的悬崖之上。"她停顿了一下。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]塔莉亚没有再催她往下说。"我没工夫听你讲故事。我离家已耽搁太久。"她转身匆匆前行，却发现那女人已在她前头。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"这片海之名，取自他的悲伤。一位伟大的国王，凡他所求皆得应许。而他登上塔梯，只为纵身跃入下方拍岸的大海，以求一死。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"这与我何干？国王来来去去；一切生灵皆有苦楚。我必须回到我的族人身边，他们正与一个威胁着日光之下每一个生灵的祸患抗争！"她脚边的尘土旋卷而起，绕着她打转，挡住了那老妇，塔莉亚再度转身向家的方向走去。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]这一次，她看见那女人从虚空中一步踏出，拦在她面前。"是何等巨大的悲伤，令他鄙弃自己的性命？你难道不知道这个故事？"老妪直视塔莉亚的双眼，这一次塔莉亚迎上了她的目光。"他最为珍视之物，被证明是虚假的。一个承诺，原来是谎言。一位妻子，原来不忠。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"魂灵，退去！别……别评判我。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"这位国王最大的心愿，便是他所信任的王后忠贞地伴他身侧，助他公正地治国。他太过仁慈，不忍将她逐走；太过明智，无法再度信她；又太过理想主义，无法在梦想遥不可及之下苟活。死亡是他所能企及的唯一解脱。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"他若从未得知此事，那便好了，"塔莉亚轻声说道。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"他会得知的，"老妪说道。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"他理应……他可以另娶。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]"他太过忠贞，做不出那种事。这位国王无法快乐……只要那背叛他的王后还活着，便不能。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]老妇转过身去，将塔莉亚从她的注视中释放。塔莉亚摇了摇头，随即转身，朝家的方向跑去。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]那老妪古朽的容貌渐渐褪去。她从袍中取出一面小镜，撒了些粉末于其上，映出一座地狱般景致中的阴郁城堡。"种子已经种下，莱丝。跟着这一个。以她的愧疚与痛楚作为祭品，将她引入你的怀抱。"[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]随后，向那逃去的塔莉亚投去最后一瞥，奥斯·加贝拉念出一句奥术咒令，返回了她的宫殿。
