CIV4GameText_MinorLeaders.xml	TXT_KEY_LEADER_MERESIN_PEDIA	Meresin appears in the official Scenarios.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][TAB]Also known as Father Whisper. Meresin was the headmaster of an orphanage and horribly mistreated the children in his care. He would offer the services of his orphanage to surrounding cities and then claim that the children had run away when most were locked beneath the orphanage until they no longer amused him, and then burnt alive in the ophanage's crematorium. He would use a barbed flail on the children, and occasionally himself.[PARAGRAPH:1]Though he was investigated, and a few children came close to escaping, Meresin was never caught and he tortured and killed hundreds of children in his life. It wasn't until a plague spread through the city, and Meresin began collecting the newly orphaned (and sick) children that he also contracted the plague that killed him. Then the town found the cellar where children were still caged and the floor was covered with ash and bones.[PARAGRAPH:1]The orphanage is still haunted by the spirits of the children that died there. Ghosts that linger in the crematorium and a Caller in the Darkness that dwells in the cellar. Children that pass too close to the ruins (especially at night) are drawn to them. An elohim priestess attempted to sanctify the ruins the the Age of Rebirth but was killed in the attempt and now her spirit wanders the area trying to find someone else to break the curse.[PARAGRAPH:1]After his death Meresin became a demon, his focus is on runaways. He is the voice that calls from the shadows, the comfort for the lost, and the voice that stokes the flames of anger and rebellion against parents. He still carries his barbed flail. If Meresin is summoned he can curse enemies with a disease that causes them to sweat blood or invoke feelings of lust, but he requires a living child in trade.	梅尔森在官方剧本中登场。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][TAB]又名“低语神父”。梅尔森曾是一家孤儿院的院长，对他照管的孩子极尽虐待。他会把孤儿院的“服务”提供给周边城镇，随后声称孩子们逃走了，而事实上大多数孩子被关押在孤儿院地下，直到再也无法取悦他，便被活活烧死在孤儿院的焚化炉里。他会用带倒刺的连枷抽打孩子，偶尔也抽打自己。[PARAGRAPH:1]尽管有人对他展开过调查，也有几个孩子险些逃脱，梅尔森却始终未被抓获，他一生折磨并杀害了数百名儿童。直到一场瘟疫在城中蔓延，梅尔森开始收留新近失去双亲（且染病）的孩子，这才染上瘟疫，命丧于此。随后镇上的人发现了那间地窖，里面仍关着被囚的孩子，地面上覆满灰烬与骸骨。[PARAGRAPH:1]那座孤儿院至今仍被死在那里的孩子们的亡魂萦绕。有徘徊在焚化炉里的幽灵，还有栖身地窖中的“黑暗召唤者”。凡是靠得太近废墟的孩子（尤其在夜里）都会被它们吸引过去。一位埃洛希姆女祭司曾在重生纪元试图净化这片废墟，却在过程中丧命，如今她的灵魂在此地游荡，想找到另一个能破除诅咒的人。[PARAGRAPH:1]梅尔森死后成了恶魔，他专注于离家出走者。他是从阴影中呼唤的声音，是迷途者的慰藉，也是那煽动怒火、教唆孩子背叛父母的声音。他仍握着那把带倒刺的连枷。若召唤梅尔森，他能以令敌人渗出血汗的疾病诅咒他们，或勾起他们的淫欲，但他索要一个活着的孩子作为交换。
CIV4GameText_MinorLeaders.xml	TXT_KEY_LEADER_KOUN_PEDIA	Minister Koun can enter the game after an Event in which a City requests freedom from your Civilization. There is a 50% chance for him to either start out on the Mother Civilization's Team, or independent (chance is determined at the start of the game). The Event to bring Minister Koun into the game will only appear in approximately 1/3 of all games played. All attributes of Minister Koun except his Traits will be based on the Mother Civilization (thus he shares the same Unique Buildings, Unique Units, Civilization Trait and World Spell). He will start in control of the Liberated City with 4 Archers and 1 Worker. Minister Koun appears in the official Scenarios and  can also lead a revolution if the Revolutions Gameoption is enabled.	权臣寇恩会在一场“某城市请求脱离你的文明”的事件之后进入游戏。他有 50% 的概率或是站在母文明一方开局，或是独立开局（该概率在游戏开始时确定）。将权臣寇恩带入游戏的事件仅在约 1/3 的对局中出现。除特性外，权臣寇恩的所有属性都以母文明为基础（因此他共享相同的特色建筑、特色单位、文明特性与世界法术）。他将掌控那座获得解放的城市开局，麾下有 4 名弓箭手和 1 名工人。权臣寇恩在官方剧本中登场，若启用“革命”游戏选项也可领导一场革命。
CIV4GameText_MinorLeaders.xml	TXT_KEY_LEADER_OUZZA_PEDIA	Ouzza appears in the official Scenarios.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][TAB]When Asmodey required the sacrifice of a child from every village, Ouzza's village (including his own father) offered him to curry favor with the powerful duke. First his mind was sacrificed by forcing him to imbibe a consecrated bottle of blood god wine, then his body was sacrificed, piece by piece. Finally, while he lay dying his soul was sacrificed to Agares.[PARAGRAPH:1]Agares accepted the gift. And eventually Ouzza returned as a demon to claim a part of the villagers that so easily offered him up. From some a tongue, from others an eye, from some, a portion of their mind or soul.[PARAGRAPH:1]In battle, Ouzza can summon serpents from inside the body of living targets and his gaze causes paralysis. He carries a bloody machete with which he can remove limbs and a ritual knife for removing internal organs, which he usually does while his victims are still alive and paralyzed. Ouzza's magic will not work on those willing to sacrifice themselves to save others.[PARAGRAPH:1]Ouzza (who is also known as the Call of the Altar or Fleshcaller) answers prayers from those who have lost a body part and he can provide a replacement, though a corrupt version, and he expects a personal sacrifice of some type from the one calling him.	领主瞿札在官方剧本中登场。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][TAB]当阿斯莫迪要求每座村庄献上一名孩童时，瞿札所在的村庄（连同他自己的父亲）为讨好这位强大的公爵，把他献了出去。先是逼他饮下一瓶被祝圣过的血神之酒，献祭了他的心智；接着，他的身体被一块块地献祭。最后，在他奄奄一息之际，他的灵魂被献给了阿加雷斯。[PARAGRAPH:1]阿加雷斯收下了这份供奉。终有一日，瞿札化作恶魔归来，向那些如此轻易将他献出的村民索取自己的一份——从某些人身上取走一条舌头，从另一些人身上取走一只眼睛，从某些人身上取走一部分心智或灵魂。[PARAGRAPH:1]战斗中，瞿札能从活着的目标体内召唤出毒蛇，他的凝视会令人瘫痪。他携带一把血淋淋的砍刀，可用来砍下肢体，还有一把用于取出内脏的仪式匕首——他通常趁受害者仍活着且瘫痪时动手。瞿札的魔法对那些甘愿牺牲自己以拯救他人的人不起作用。[PARAGRAPH:1]瞿札（又名“祭坛的呼唤”或“唤肉者”）会回应那些失去了某个身体部位之人的祈祷，他能提供替代之物，尽管是被扭曲的版本，而且他期望呼唤他的人作出某种个人牺牲。
