Civ4GameText_Advanced_Diplomacy.xml	TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_ADVANCED_DIPLOMACY_PEDIA	[H1]Advanced Diplomacy[\\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Advanced Diplomacy (enabled via the Advanced tactics option) vastly changes the way diplomacy works from standard Civilization. Many new trading options are added, each with their own benefits, and potiential disadvantages. What follows is a list of the new options. (Warning: incomplete)[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]Embassies.[\\BOLD] Nations can now establish embassies in other nations. Embassies improve diplomatic relations between countries over time, but be warned; revoking a foreign embassies rights will have disastrous diplomatic repercussions with the other nation. Embassies are now required to unlock higher diplomatic functions with other nations, namely, [COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]Open Borders Agreements[COLOR_REVERT], [COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]Defensive Pacts[COLOR_REVERT], and some new options (see below). Requires [LINK=TECH_WRITING]Writing[\\LINK].[PARAGRAPH:2] [BOLD]Right of Passage.[\\BOLD] Similar to open borders, in that it allows foreign trade, but the agreement only allows for defensive units and scouts to pass through the nations. Other units will not be able to enter the territory. Requires [LINK=TECH_WRITING]Writing[\\LINK].[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]Free Trade Agreement.[\\BOLD] This agreement increases gold from trading missions and improves diplomatic relations over time. Requires [LINK=TECH_WRITING]Writing[\\LINK] and [COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]Open borders[COLOR_REVERT].[PARAGRAPH:2] [BOLD]Non-Aggression Pact.[\\BOLD] The AI is somewhat less likely to attack a player with whom it has a non-agression pact. Also improves diplomatic relations over time. Requires [LINK=TECH_WRITING]Writing[\\LINK] and [COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]Embassy[COLOR_REVERT].[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]Trading Military Units and Workers.[\\BOLD] Workers and certain Military units, like siege machines, can be traded. Each tradable unit will be marked in it's respective civilopedia entry with &quot;This unit is tradable.&quot; Requires [COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]Embassy[COLOR_REVERT].	[H1]高级外交[\\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]高级外交（通过“高级战术”选项启用）极大地改变了外交在标准文明中的运作方式。新增了许多贸易选项，各有其收益，也各有潜在的弊端。下面列出这些新选项。（警告：尚不完整）[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]大使馆。[\\BOLD]各国如今可以在他国设立大使馆。大使馆会随时间改善两国间的外交关系，但请注意：撤销外国大使馆的权利会给与该国的外交带来灾难性的后果。如今，要解锁与他国更高级的外交功能——即[COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]开放边境协定[COLOR_REVERT]、[COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]防御同盟[COLOR_REVERT]以及一些新选项（见下文）——都需要先设立大使馆。需要[LINK=TECH_WRITING]文字[\\LINK]。[PARAGRAPH:2] [BOLD]通行权。[\\BOLD]与开放边境类似，同样允许外国通行，但该协定只允许防御单位和侦察兵通过本国领土。其他单位无法进入。需要[LINK=TECH_WRITING]文字[\\LINK]。[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]自由贸易协定。[\\BOLD]该协定提升贸易任务所得的金钱，并随时间改善外交关系。需要[LINK=TECH_WRITING]文字[\\LINK]与[COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]开放边境[COLOR_REVERT]。[PARAGRAPH:2] [BOLD]互不侵犯条约。[\\BOLD]AI 攻击与其签有互不侵犯条约的玩家的可能性会略微降低，同时也随时间改善外交关系。需要[LINK=TECH_WRITING]文字[\\LINK]与[COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]大使馆[COLOR_REVERT]。[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]交易军事单位与工人。[\\BOLD]工人以及某些军事单位（如攻城器械）可被交易。每种可交易的单位都会在其对应的文明百科条目中标注&quot;此单位可被交易。&quot;需要[COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]大使馆[COLOR_REVERT]。
