Civ4GameText_Advanced_Diplomacy.xml	TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_ACTIVE_SENATE_PEDIA	[H1]Active Senate[\\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Under some types of government ([LINK=CIVIC_REPRESENTATION]Representation[\\LINK], [LINK=CIVIC_UNIVERSAL_SUFFRAGE]Universal Suffrage[\\LINK]), the Senate can interfere with your military policy. Thus, it may invalidate your declarations of war and/or force you to sign a peace treaty with your enemies.[PARAGRAPH:2]The decisions of the Senate depend in particular on the scale of the conflict, either potential or actual, and its real interest. Thus, pursue a policy military under democratic regime becomes more difficult.[PARAGRAPH:2] However, when an opponent make unpleasant acts to your nation, by a embargo, a negative vote, an espionage mission, etc. ..., you have a sufficient pretext to go to war without Senate intervention. Any war pretext is valid for one turn and throughout the conflict in case of a declaration of war. Of course, malicious acts of enemies who are already at war against you are a pretext to circumvent the Senate.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]	[H1]活跃元老院[\\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]在某些政体下（[LINK=CIVIC_REPRESENTATION]代议制[\\LINK]、[LINK=CIVIC_UNIVERSAL_SUFFRAGE]普选制[\\LINK]），元老院会干预你的军事政策。因此，它可能否决你的宣战，或迫使你与敌人签订和约。[PARAGRAPH:2]元老院的决定尤其取决于冲突的规模（无论是潜在的还是实际的）及其切身利益。因此，在民主政体下推行军事政策会变得更加困难。[PARAGRAPH:2]然而，当对手对你的国家做出不友善的举动，例如禁运、投反对票、间谍任务等等，你便有充分的借口不经元老院干预即可开战。任何开战借口在一个回合内有效，且在宣战情形下贯穿整场冲突。当然，已经对你开战之敌的恶意举动，本身就是绕开元老院的借口。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]
