Civ4GameText_Advanced_Diplomacy.xml	TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_CONDAMN_CIVIC_PEDIA	[H1]Condamned Civic[\\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]The United Nations can vote on resolution of condemnation of a civic. If and only if this civic is adopted by one of the voting players. Are condemnable by the United Nations, some of the most extremist civics. [PARAGRAPH:2]Choosing a condemned civic generate a diplomatic penalty from the voting members and exclude the civilization to the clan of members which can vote, which in itself is not always a bad thing (as you assess the risks and benefits of such a situation.)[PARAGRAPH:2]It is possible that a AI player proposes such a resolution and pass it, in which case it can influence the course of the game. But from a human point of view, the interest is more subtile. It allows to turn some civilizations against another. Indeed, if you want to attack an opponent who has a state religion shared by you and your allies, but he chose a different religious doctrine, you can try to condemn it to make it a pariat and attack without offending your brothers in faith, even with their assistance.[PARAGRAPH:2]From a historical point of view, the interest is basically to be able to condemn the reform among others.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]	[H1]受谴责政策[\\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]联合国可以就谴责某项政策的决议进行投票。当且仅当该政策被某个参与投票的玩家采用时方可谴责。可被联合国谴责的，是一些最为极端的政策。[PARAGRAPH:2]选择受谴责政策会招致投票成员的外交惩罚，并将该文明排除在可投票的成员集团之外——这本身未必是坏事（你需要权衡此种处境的风险与收益）。[PARAGRAPH:2]AI 玩家有可能提出并通过这样的决议，此时它会影响游戏进程。但从人类玩家的角度看，其意义更为微妙。它可以使某些文明反目成仇。事实上，如果你想攻击一个与你及盟友共享国教、却选择了不同宗教教义的对手，你可以设法谴责它，使其沦为弃儿，从而在不冒犯信仰弟兄的情况下发动攻击，甚至得到他们的协助。[PARAGRAPH:2]从历史角度看，其意义主要在于能够谴责诸如改革之类的政策。[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]
